WEBVTT

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.883
Ship is gray, Captain.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.444
We've cut power
to Decks 4 through 9.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.820
Replicators, holodecks,

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.348
and all other nonessentials
are off-line.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.328
Remaining systems are operating
at 20 percent capacity.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.331
Tom, how long
can you keep us flying?

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.492
With the deuterium supply
this low,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.229
even at one-quarter impulse,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.430
we'll be out of gas
inside a week.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.098
Everyone redouble your efforts.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.700
Keep your eyes open
for new sources of deuterium.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.370
Tuvok, Chakotay,
l want recommendations

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.437
for further methods
of conservation.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.643
Harry, you and l will
give them a hand in Geophysics...

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.675
see if we can't synthesize
a substitute fuel.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.779
In the meantime,
we stay in gray mode.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.450
If anybody's got
any other ideas, l'm listening.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.186
We could set up a bicycle

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.389
in the Mess Hall,
attach a generator, pedal home.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.863
Now, why didn't l think of that?

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.527
And l volunteer Harry
to take the first shift.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.832
Living space will
be extremely limited.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:18.970
Take only those personal items
which are absolutely essential.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.673
Hello, there!

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.517
What, may l ask, is this?

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:31.650
That, Mr. Vulcan,
is the Selected Works of Jirex.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.420
Only essential items,
Mr. Neelix.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.757
Oh, Jirex is essential.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.228
He's the greatest writer
in the Talaxian canon.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.560
L never go to sleep

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.896
without reading at least
one of his parables.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.265
A habit you will have to break,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.566
until we're able to restore
power to crew quarters.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.834
L suppose l can try.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.000
And... these?

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:52.500
I... l get terrible
neck pains without them.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.671
L suggest you ask the Doctor

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.146
to prescribe
an anti-inflammatory.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.742
Oh, fine.
L don't mind roughing it.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.449
Mr. Neelix, the blankets.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.685
No. No, that's
where l draw the line.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.625
My mother
knitted these herself.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.128
L've slept with them
since l was a child.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.563
You'll have to make do
with standard-issue bedding.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.227
But those Starfleet blankets
give me a rash.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.860
Then l suggest you
ask the Doctor...

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.200
For some anti-itch cream.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.899
L might as well sleep
in Sick Bay!

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.909
Thank you, Mr. Vulcan.
You've just given me an idea.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.612
What's going on here?

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.815
L'm working.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.120
You were ordered to shut down
Astrometrics an hour ago.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.922
We can't afford the power.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.985
Seven, it's inefficient.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.087
Efficiency is relative,
Commander.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.359
If l shut down Astrometrics,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.390
l won't be able to scan
for new fuel sources.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.924
L appreciate your efforts,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.903
but we'll have to use
conventional scanners until...

00:02:57.043 --> 00:03:00.012
Conventional scanners
would not have found this.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.343
What?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.281
Highly concentrated deuterium.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.783
Where?

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.910
Computer, display source.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:10.411
A planetoid.4 light-years
from our present position.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.924
There are dense
pockets of deuterium

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.256
just beneath the surface.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.626
Maybe so, but that's
a Demon-class planet.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.960
Demon-class?

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.760
That's what Starfleet calls it.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.289
Also known as Class-Y.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.858
It's got a toxic atmosphere

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.767
filled with
thermionic radiation.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.602
Surface temperatures are
in excess of 500 Kelvins.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.370
Just entering a standard
orbit would be suicide.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.502
Our situation is desperate.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.704
True.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:36.841
When faced with desperate
circumstances, we must adapt.

00:05:28.593 --> 00:05:30.618
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:05:30.661 --> 00:05:32.595
L've ordered adaptations
to our shields

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.098
to repel
the thermionic discharges.

00:05:35.132 --> 00:05:37.566
Hoping that the benefits
will outweigh the risks,

00:05:37.602 --> 00:05:39.399
we're now trying
to beam deuterium

00:05:39.437 --> 00:05:41.337
from beneath
the planet's surface.

00:05:41.372 --> 00:05:44.569
Narrow the annular confinement
beam to.47 terahertz.

00:05:44.609 --> 00:05:46.270
Ready here, Captain.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.436
Stand by.

00:05:47.478 --> 00:05:49.571
Harry, shunt whatever
additional power you can

00:05:49.614 --> 00:05:50.876
to the containment field.

00:05:50.915 --> 00:05:53.975
L don't want any of those
atmospheric gases seeping in.

00:05:54.018 --> 00:05:55.349
Aye, Captain.

00:05:55.386 --> 00:05:58.355
A thermionic discharge
has struck the forward shields.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:05:59.856
They're holding.

00:05:59.891 --> 00:06:02.086
Let's get this over with
before you tell me otherwise.

00:06:02.126 --> 00:06:03.388
Seven, do it.

00:06:03.427 --> 00:06:04.689
Energize.

00:06:08.332 --> 00:06:10.800
Transport in progress.

00:06:12.603 --> 00:06:14.434
Shields are weakening.

00:06:14.472 --> 00:06:16.201
L'm reading an overload
in the pattern buffers.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.537
Abort transport.

00:06:17.575 --> 00:06:18.940
Controls not responding!

00:06:18.976 --> 00:06:20.034
Get out of there now.

00:06:25.016 --> 00:06:26.608
Computer, seal off
the Transporter Room

00:06:26.651 --> 00:06:29.620
and erect
a level-10 containment field.

00:06:29.654 --> 00:06:31.383
Containment field established.

00:06:34.825 --> 00:06:36.452
The good news is
Nozawa and Seven of Nine

00:06:36.494 --> 00:06:39.054
have both been treated
and released from Sick Bay,

00:06:39.096 --> 00:06:40.961
and the planetary gases
have been expelled

00:06:41.032 --> 00:06:42.397
from the transporter room.

00:06:42.433 --> 00:06:43.730
And the bad news?

00:06:43.768 --> 00:06:45.258
The transporters are off-line.

00:06:45.303 --> 00:06:46.702
It'll take days
before they're back again.

00:06:46.737 --> 00:06:49.433
Great. We lose valuable
energy on a course change,

00:06:49.473 --> 00:06:52.067
and all we get for our trouble
is another downed system.

00:06:52.109 --> 00:06:55.078
Can we send a probe
to collect the deuterium?

00:06:55.112 --> 00:06:56.841
Lt would incinerate
within seconds

00:06:56.881 --> 00:06:58.576
of entering
the upper atmosphere.

00:06:58.616 --> 00:07:00.982
Then l don't see
any other options.

00:07:01.052 --> 00:07:03.350
Tom, put us back
on our original course.

00:07:03.387 --> 00:07:04.684
One-quarter impulse.

00:07:04.722 --> 00:07:06.519
Captain, maybe l can help.

00:07:06.557 --> 00:07:09.526
Harry, the bicycle thing
was just a joke.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.857
L've been thinking.

00:07:10.895 --> 00:07:12.886
With Tuvok's shield
modifications

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.490
and a few tweaks
to an environmental suit,

00:07:15.533 --> 00:07:16.864
l could take a shuttle
to the surface

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:18.664
and mine the deuterium
from there.

00:07:18.703 --> 00:07:21.638
Need l remind you, Ensign,
that there is no environment

00:07:21.672 --> 00:07:24.334
less hospitable to humanoid life
than a Class-Y.

00:07:24.375 --> 00:07:26.707
Actually, Tuvok, no,
you needn't remind me.

00:07:26.744 --> 00:07:28.644
What's the alternative?

00:07:28.679 --> 00:07:30.306
Resume course, creep
along at quarter-impulse

00:07:30.348 --> 00:07:31.576
hoping we'll find fuel

00:07:31.616 --> 00:07:33.106
before we end up
dead in the water?

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:35.675
We've got deuterium
within arm's reach.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.312
We can't let the
opportunity slip away

00:07:37.355 --> 00:07:38.379
without at least trying.

00:07:38.422 --> 00:07:39.719
He's got a point.

00:07:39.757 --> 00:07:41.247
You wouldn't be able
to communicate with us

00:07:41.292 --> 00:07:42.554
if you got in trouble.

00:07:42.593 --> 00:07:43.958
And until
we can get transporters back,

00:07:43.995 --> 00:07:45.053
we couldn't beam you out.

00:07:45.096 --> 00:07:47.189
Even with modifications,

00:07:47.231 --> 00:07:49.699
it wouldn't be long before
your suit began to corrode.

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:52.396
Exposure to that atmosphere
could kill you within minutes.

00:07:52.436 --> 00:07:53.869
L know the risks.

00:07:53.904 --> 00:07:56.304
Even if l agreed,
l'd never let you go alone.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.637
Of course not.

00:07:57.675 --> 00:07:58.733
That's why l'm volunteering

00:07:58.776 --> 00:08:00.334
my good buddy Tom
here to go with me.

00:08:06.751 --> 00:08:08.685
You were pretty forceful
in there.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:10.016
So?

00:08:10.054 --> 00:08:11.351
So? L don't think

00:08:11.389 --> 00:08:13.323
l've ever seen you
that assertive

00:08:13.357 --> 00:08:14.847
in a staff meeting before.

00:08:14.892 --> 00:08:17.019
You must be bucking
for a promotion.

00:08:17.061 --> 00:08:19.154
L had an idea
and l spoke up, that's all.

00:08:19.196 --> 00:08:21.221
Oh, no, no, no.
It was more than that.

00:08:21.265 --> 00:08:24.530
You put Tuvok in his place,
right in front of everybody.

00:08:24.568 --> 00:08:26.263
He was stating
the obvious again.

00:08:26.303 --> 00:08:27.930
Talking down to me
like l didn't

00:08:27.972 --> 00:08:30.031
know anything
about Demon-class planets?

00:08:30.074 --> 00:08:31.632
L am not criticizing you.

00:08:31.676 --> 00:08:33.701
Believe me, nobody enjoys seeing

00:08:33.744 --> 00:08:36.941
the Vulcan master put down a peg
more than l do.

00:08:37.014 --> 00:08:39.380
L was just surprised,
that's all.

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:40.884
Why?

00:08:40.918 --> 00:08:42.579
Lt didn't seem like you.

00:08:43.587 --> 00:08:45.054
Good.

00:08:47.425 --> 00:08:49.791
Cargo Bay 2.

00:08:49.827 --> 00:08:52.352
You trying to change

00:08:52.396 --> 00:08:54.227
your squeaky-clean image
or something?

00:08:54.265 --> 00:08:56.256
Not exactly.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.200
What, then?

00:08:58.235 --> 00:09:00.066
How do l explain this?

00:09:02.473 --> 00:09:04.304
When l first
came on board Voyager,

00:09:04.341 --> 00:09:06.138
l was pretty green, right?

00:09:07.178 --> 00:09:10.306
A deep,
almost fluorescent green,

00:09:10.347 --> 00:09:12.247
if l remember correctly.

00:09:12.283 --> 00:09:15.844
L was young, inexperienced,
and l acted like it...

00:09:15.886 --> 00:09:19.083
nervous about giving my opinion,
hesitant to make suggestions...

00:09:19.123 --> 00:09:22.217
so l usually just
kept my mouth shut,

00:09:22.259 --> 00:09:24.659
and l behaved that way
for so long,

00:09:24.695 --> 00:09:26.390
it became a habit.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:31.026
But, in the last four years,
a lot has happened.

00:09:31.068 --> 00:09:33.468
L've fought the Borg,

00:09:33.504 --> 00:09:35.404
been transformed into an alien,

00:09:35.439 --> 00:09:36.804
helped defeat the Hirogen.

00:09:36.841 --> 00:09:38.638
Hell, l've even
come back from the dead.

00:09:39.677 --> 00:09:41.076
It's been a wild ride.

00:09:41.112 --> 00:09:44.104
L woke up the other morning
and it suddenly hit me...

00:09:44.148 --> 00:09:46.582
l've got a lot
of experience now,

00:09:46.617 --> 00:09:47.948
so why should l be afraid

00:09:48.052 --> 00:09:51.647
to take the initiative
or voice my ideas?

00:09:53.457 --> 00:09:55.584
Good for you, Harry.

00:09:55.626 --> 00:09:56.615
But...

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:57.957
do me a favor.

00:09:57.995 --> 00:10:00.054
The next time you try
to assert yourself,

00:10:00.097 --> 00:10:01.394
leave me out of it.

00:10:01.432 --> 00:10:02.729
L hate hot weather.

00:10:02.767 --> 00:10:04.166
Don't worry,
we can cut some holes

00:10:04.201 --> 00:10:06.897
in the environmental suits,
get some ventilation going.

00:10:06.937 --> 00:10:10.373
Harry, while you're
busy improving yourself,

00:10:10.407 --> 00:10:12.068
you might try working
on your sense of humor.

00:10:12.109 --> 00:10:13.406
My sense of humor?

00:10:13.444 --> 00:10:15.742
What about that stupid gag
about the bicycle?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.077
Oh, ho-ho!
That was funny.

00:10:17.114 --> 00:10:18.445
No, that was not funny.

00:10:18.482 --> 00:10:19.847
You think that's humor?

00:10:27.024 --> 00:10:28.423
L can't thank you enough

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:29.983
for getting me in
on this mission, Harry.

00:10:30.094 --> 00:10:31.994
Don't mention it.

00:10:32.029 --> 00:10:33.997
Remind me
to volunteer you to help

00:10:34.031 --> 00:10:37.330
the next time l have to clean
the warp plasma manifolds.

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:39.632
Really, Tom,
you don't owe me anything.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.297
Oh, but l do.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.566
We've lost attitude control.

00:10:44.608 --> 00:10:47.008
Time to show off
your piloting skills.

00:10:47.077 --> 00:10:48.669
Think you can handle it?

00:10:48.712 --> 00:10:50.646
Watch me.

00:10:50.681 --> 00:10:52.512
Oh, l'll be watching you,
all right.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.017
Switching to manual control.

00:10:54.084 --> 00:10:58.145
Just sit back, relax,
and enjoy the ride.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.024
We're entering
the lower atmosphere,

00:11:02.059 --> 00:11:04.084
approaching
the landing coordinates.

00:11:04.128 --> 00:11:07.393
All right.
L'm going to set us down.

00:11:07.431 --> 00:11:09.092
On my mark...

00:11:14.104 --> 00:11:15.969
Mark.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.031
You did that on purpose,
didn't you?

00:11:27.618 --> 00:11:31.076
Lt's almost 500 degrees Kelvin.

00:11:31.121 --> 00:11:35.080
Don't worry.
The suits can handle it.

00:11:35.125 --> 00:11:39.118
If not, we'll be human barbecue.

00:11:41.131 --> 00:11:45.124
L'm picking up
traces of deuterium...

00:11:45.169 --> 00:11:47.603
50 meters... that way.

00:11:47.638 --> 00:11:49.105
Let's move.

00:11:49.139 --> 00:11:50.606
No sweat.

00:11:50.641 --> 00:11:52.108
Lame.

00:12:05.923 --> 00:12:08.721
It's coming from in here.

00:12:08.759 --> 00:12:11.557
What is it?

00:12:11.595 --> 00:12:14.894
Some kind of metallic
compound...

00:12:14.932 --> 00:12:18.060
highly viscous...

00:12:18.102 --> 00:12:20.502
and if these readings are right,

00:12:20.537 --> 00:12:23.404
its temperature
is only 12 degrees?!

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.135
In this environment?!

00:12:25.175 --> 00:12:26.472
Whatever this stuff is,

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.612
it's packed
with liquefied deuterium.

00:12:28.745 --> 00:12:29.905
Jackpot.

00:12:29.946 --> 00:12:31.243
There's another pool

00:12:31.281 --> 00:12:32.145
20 meters that way.

00:12:32.182 --> 00:12:33.581
Why don't you go check it out

00:12:33.617 --> 00:12:35.346
while l collect
a few samples here.

00:12:35.385 --> 00:12:36.511
Right.

00:12:36.553 --> 00:12:39.784
L don't know, Harry...

00:12:39.823 --> 00:12:42.257
a couple of lounge chairs,

00:12:42.292 --> 00:12:44.760
a big beach umbrella,

00:12:44.794 --> 00:12:47.228
maybe some dermalplast to
counteract the chemical burns,

00:12:47.263 --> 00:12:49.959
and l think we've found
ourselves a new vacation spot.

00:12:52.369 --> 00:12:53.461
Aw, come on.

00:12:53.503 --> 00:12:54.492
That was a little funny.

00:12:54.537 --> 00:12:55.834
Let me hear you do better.

00:13:00.076 --> 00:13:01.566
Harry?

00:13:07.584 --> 00:13:09.074
Harry!

00:13:16.726 --> 00:13:18.455
Oh, my God.

00:13:34.177 --> 00:13:35.769
L know it's hot out, Harry,

00:13:35.812 --> 00:13:38.576
but you picked a lousy time
to go for a swim.

00:13:38.615 --> 00:13:40.708
L don't know what happened.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.344
L leaned over
to collect a sample

00:13:43.386 --> 00:13:45.911
and it was like l was pulled in.

00:13:45.955 --> 00:13:47.422
Warning. Ensign Kim,

00:13:47.457 --> 00:13:50.654
an environmental seal
has been compromised.

00:13:50.694 --> 00:13:52.787
Oxygen depletion in 30 seconds.

00:13:55.632 --> 00:13:57.122
Hang in there, buddy,

00:13:57.167 --> 00:13:59.533
and l'll get you back
to the shuttle.

00:14:01.071 --> 00:14:03.039
Have you put on weight?

00:14:03.073 --> 00:14:04.404
You're just out of shape.

00:14:04.441 --> 00:14:05.601
Warning.

00:14:05.642 --> 00:14:09.203
Oxygen depletion in 15 seconds.

00:14:09.245 --> 00:14:11.713
L'll make you a deal...
you hold your breath

00:14:11.748 --> 00:14:12.874
till we get back
to the shuttle,

00:14:12.916 --> 00:14:15.043
and l promise l'll start
exercising every day.

00:14:15.085 --> 00:14:17.815
Maybe you should start
with the bicycle.

00:14:17.854 --> 00:14:19.321
L thought l told you
to hold your breath.

00:14:21.191 --> 00:14:24.456
Warning. Oxygen depletion
in five seconds.

00:14:28.098 --> 00:14:29.565
Hang in there, Harry.

00:14:29.599 --> 00:14:31.089
We'll make it.

00:14:32.535 --> 00:14:34.867
Warning. Lieutenant Paris,

00:14:34.904 --> 00:14:37.566
an environmental seal
has been compromised.

00:14:37.607 --> 00:14:39.802
Oxygen depletion in 30 seconds.

00:14:43.279 --> 00:14:44.769
You gotta be kidding me.

00:14:46.616 --> 00:14:48.641
We're in the same boat now,
buddy,

00:14:48.685 --> 00:14:50.346
but l'll get us out of this.

00:14:51.554 --> 00:14:55.115
Warning.
Oxygen depletion in 15 seconds.

00:14:56.459 --> 00:14:58.484
You're right.

00:14:58.528 --> 00:15:00.962
L definitely need
to get back in shape.

00:15:00.997 --> 00:15:04.660
Warning. Oxygen depletion
in five seconds.

00:15:20.984 --> 00:15:22.383
Out of the question.

00:15:22.418 --> 00:15:23.885
Be reasonable, Doctor.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.683
Take it up
with Commander Chakotay.

00:15:25.722 --> 00:15:27.280
He's on his way
here right now.

00:15:27.323 --> 00:15:29.086
But it's only
for a couple of days.

00:15:29.125 --> 00:15:31.855
Just until we get power back
in the crew quarters.

00:15:31.895 --> 00:15:34.193
L suggest you set up camp
in the Mess Hall.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.458
The Mess Hall is full.

00:15:35.498 --> 00:15:37.261
Where are we
supposed to sleep?

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.358
Anywhere but here.

00:15:38.401 --> 00:15:40.266
This is a Sick Bay,
not a dormitory.

00:15:40.303 --> 00:15:42.294
But you have four empty beds.

00:15:42.338 --> 00:15:44.169
Bio-beds, reserved for patients.

00:15:44.207 --> 00:15:44.969
You don't have any patients.

00:15:45.041 --> 00:15:46.633
L may have one in a moment,

00:15:46.676 --> 00:15:49.338
if you and your fellow squatters
don't go elsewhere.

00:15:49.379 --> 00:15:51.176
You wanted to see me, Doctor?

00:15:51.214 --> 00:15:52.340
Oh, it's about time.

00:15:52.382 --> 00:15:54.475
Mr. Neelix is attempting
to turn my Sick Bay

00:15:54.517 --> 00:15:55.541
into a flophouse.

00:15:55.585 --> 00:15:56.984
We are short on beds for now.

00:15:57.086 --> 00:15:58.075
We've got to adapt.

00:15:58.121 --> 00:15:58.951
Aha.

00:15:58.988 --> 00:16:00.683
But what if there's

00:16:00.723 --> 00:16:02.554
a medical emergency?

00:16:02.592 --> 00:16:04.651
Then Neelix and the others
will get out of the way.

00:16:04.694 --> 00:16:06.161
Absolutely.

00:16:06.196 --> 00:16:08.790
But... this isn't just Sick Bay.

00:16:08.832 --> 00:16:10.322
It's my residence.

00:16:10.366 --> 00:16:13.733
And we promise to be
the most perfect houseguests.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.294
What more can you ask for?

00:16:15.338 --> 00:16:16.305
But...

00:16:16.339 --> 00:16:17.931
l have a routine.

00:16:18.007 --> 00:16:20.237
L'm a night owl.

00:16:20.276 --> 00:16:21.573
What if one of them should snore

00:16:21.611 --> 00:16:22.942
while l'm listening to Puccini?

00:16:22.979 --> 00:16:25.106
Well, if you feel
that strongly about it, Doc,

00:16:25.148 --> 00:16:27.343
l suppose we'll have to consider
other options.

00:16:27.383 --> 00:16:29.112
Thank you, Commander.

00:16:29.152 --> 00:16:31.279
For example, we could
shut down your program

00:16:31.321 --> 00:16:32.310
until you're needed.

00:16:32.355 --> 00:16:34.289
The Captain asked me
to look for ways

00:16:34.324 --> 00:16:36.588
to conserve power,
and it would spare you

00:16:36.626 --> 00:16:38.457
from having to listen
to them snore.

00:16:38.494 --> 00:16:40.155
Commander Chakotay
to the Bridge.

00:16:40.196 --> 00:16:41.356
On my way.

00:16:41.397 --> 00:16:42.489
But...

00:16:46.769 --> 00:16:48.964
Make yourselves at home.

00:16:49.005 --> 00:16:51.132
Try scanning
for infrared signatures.

00:16:51.174 --> 00:16:53.836
There's too much interference.

00:16:53.877 --> 00:16:54.844
What's up?

00:16:54.878 --> 00:16:56.368
Tom and Harry
still aren't back.

00:16:56.412 --> 00:16:58.539
You want me to take another
shuttle down and look for them?

00:16:58.581 --> 00:17:00.208
And risk losing you, too?

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:03.708
Either we keep waiting
until we run out or deuterium

00:17:03.753 --> 00:17:05.482
and get trapped in orbit, or...

00:17:05.521 --> 00:17:06.488
Or?

00:17:06.522 --> 00:17:07.784
We land the ship.

00:17:07.824 --> 00:17:10.156
As you know, Captain,
the landing procedure

00:17:10.193 --> 00:17:12.320
requires a significant
output of energy.

00:17:12.362 --> 00:17:13.829
With shield strength
as low as it is,

00:17:13.863 --> 00:17:14.852
we can't even be certain

00:17:14.898 --> 00:17:15.887
the ship will survive
the descent.

00:17:15.932 --> 00:17:16.921
What's the alternative?

00:17:17.033 --> 00:17:19.092
We're up here,
the deuterium's down there,

00:17:19.135 --> 00:17:20.466
and we're stuck without it.

00:17:20.503 --> 00:17:22.300
We've come this far.

00:17:22.338 --> 00:17:24.135
Janeway to Engineering.

00:17:24.173 --> 00:17:26.232
Vent all plasma
from the nacelles.

00:17:26.276 --> 00:17:29.575
Transfer any available power
to atmospheric thrusters

00:17:29.612 --> 00:17:31.842
and stand by
to commence landing sequence.

00:17:31.881 --> 00:17:32.939
Acknowledged, Captain.

00:17:33.049 --> 00:17:36.712
Commander Chakotay,
take the conn.

00:17:36.753 --> 00:17:38.948
Tom's going to be sorry
he missed this.

00:17:39.055 --> 00:17:39.953
Code Blue.

00:17:40.056 --> 00:17:41.546
Commander Tuvok to all hands.

00:17:41.591 --> 00:17:42.615
Go to Blue Alert

00:17:42.659 --> 00:17:44.820
and report
to Code Blue stations.

00:17:44.861 --> 00:17:47.125
Atmospheric controls at standby.

00:17:47.163 --> 00:17:48.790
Landing struts on line.

00:17:48.831 --> 00:17:50.822
Inertial dampers at maximum.

00:17:50.867 --> 00:17:53.199
All operative decks report
Condition Blue.

00:17:53.236 --> 00:17:55.067
Let us down easy, Commander.

00:18:05.281 --> 00:18:07.272
We're on
a declining glide trajectory.

00:18:07.317 --> 00:18:09.877
Altitude 150 kilometers.

00:18:09.919 --> 00:18:12.285
A thermionic discharge.

00:18:12.322 --> 00:18:14.381
Shields down to 81 percent.

00:18:17.961 --> 00:18:20.521
Shields at 43 percent.

00:18:20.563 --> 00:18:21.427
Chakotay.

00:18:21.464 --> 00:18:23.728
L think we're through
the worst of it.

00:18:23.766 --> 00:18:25.563
Almost.

00:18:25.601 --> 00:18:27.364
Shields at 22 percent
and falling.

00:18:27.403 --> 00:18:28.927
Can you shore them up?

00:18:28.972 --> 00:18:31.304
Negative. There's
no more available power.

00:18:31.341 --> 00:18:33.138
Engaging landing struts.

00:18:39.916 --> 00:18:41.645
Brace for impact!

00:18:47.924 --> 00:18:49.050
Status?

00:18:49.092 --> 00:18:52.289
L could give you a litany
of damaged systems, Captain,

00:18:52.328 --> 00:18:54.353
but suffice it to say,
now that we're down,

00:18:54.397 --> 00:18:55.955
we won't be going up again soon.

00:18:55.999 --> 00:18:58.695
Start organizing repair crews.

00:19:00.303 --> 00:19:03.136
Well, that was very good,
Commander.

00:19:03.172 --> 00:19:05.766
Take an away team
and find Harry and Tom.

00:19:17.253 --> 00:19:20.017
Chakotay... you're going out
to look for them, aren't you?

00:19:20.056 --> 00:19:21.489
- That's right.
- Take me with you.

00:19:21.524 --> 00:19:22.718
L can't do that, B'Elanna.

00:19:22.759 --> 00:19:24.283
You're needed here
to complete repairs.

00:19:24.327 --> 00:19:26.022
L've already handed
out assignments.

00:19:26.062 --> 00:19:27.188
Vorik's on top of it.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.822
L want to help you find them.

00:19:28.865 --> 00:19:31.095
Look... l know you're
concerned about Tom and Harry.

00:19:31.134 --> 00:19:32.226
We all are.

00:19:32.268 --> 00:19:34.293
L'll have them back
safe and sound in no time.

00:19:34.337 --> 00:19:35.326
Don't patronize me.

00:19:35.371 --> 00:19:37.362
We both know how dangerous
that environment is.

00:19:37.407 --> 00:19:38.806
They could be
in serious trouble.

00:19:38.841 --> 00:19:39.705
You're right.

00:19:39.742 --> 00:19:41.403
L don't know
what we're going to find.

00:19:41.444 --> 00:19:44.811
That's why l need cool heads.

00:19:44.847 --> 00:19:46.144
You think l can't
control myself?

00:19:46.182 --> 00:19:47.410
L think you're a little
too close to this.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:48.883
You're damn right l am.

00:19:48.918 --> 00:19:50.818
If someone you loved
was missing on this planet,

00:19:50.853 --> 00:19:53.054
you would be the first one
out that door, and you know it.

00:19:53.187 --> 00:19:54.916
B'Elanna, the clock is ticking.

00:19:54.955 --> 00:19:57.116
Go back to Engineering,
do your job,

00:19:57.158 --> 00:19:58.921
and let me do mine.

00:19:58.959 --> 00:20:00.358
Do me a favor.

00:20:00.394 --> 00:20:01.861
What?

00:20:01.896 --> 00:20:03.659
Take Seven of Nine with you.

00:20:05.099 --> 00:20:07.124
You're recommending her?

00:20:07.168 --> 00:20:09.295
You said you needed cool heads,
didn't you?

00:20:09.336 --> 00:20:11.065
Nobody's head is cooler
than hers.

00:20:13.274 --> 00:20:14.298
All right.

00:20:17.078 --> 00:20:19.012
And bring them back safe.

00:20:21.248 --> 00:20:22.715
L will.

00:20:41.769 --> 00:20:42.827
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:43.996
Yes, Mr. Neelix?

00:20:44.038 --> 00:20:46.336
We'd like to sleep now,
if you don't mind.

00:20:46.373 --> 00:20:47.340
Not at all.

00:20:47.374 --> 00:20:48.864
Make yourselves comfortable.

00:20:48.909 --> 00:20:51.139
But you seem busy.

00:20:51.178 --> 00:20:52.270
Oh, don't mind me.

00:20:52.313 --> 00:20:54.008
Just going about my routine.

00:20:54.048 --> 00:20:56.380
Sleep away.

00:21:00.921 --> 00:21:02.320
What about the lights?

00:21:02.356 --> 00:21:03.323
What about them?

00:21:03.357 --> 00:21:04.722
Could we turn them off?

00:21:04.758 --> 00:21:07.283
You don't expect me to work
in the dark, do you?

00:21:07.328 --> 00:21:08.556
Well, no,

00:21:08.596 --> 00:21:10.359
but l'll never be able
to fall asleep.

00:21:10.397 --> 00:21:12.592
That's not my problem, is it?

00:21:12.633 --> 00:21:16.569
L've got a very, very
busy day tomorrow

00:21:16.604 --> 00:21:19.903
and my next shift is
just four hours away.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:20.964
Perhaps you should've
thought of that

00:21:21.008 --> 00:21:22.771
when choosing
your accommodations.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.142
Well, if we can't sleep,

00:21:25.179 --> 00:21:29.843
l guess we'll just have
to find some other way

00:21:29.884 --> 00:21:31.977
to pass the time.

00:21:32.086 --> 00:21:35.715
How about a sing-along?

00:21:35.756 --> 00:21:39.453
L could teach you all
some Talaxian rondos,

00:21:39.493 --> 00:21:41.927
and l know
a Vulcan funeral dirge,

00:21:41.962 --> 00:21:44.658
not to mention
the classics of Klingon opera.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.225
Very well, Mr. Neelix, you win.

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:50.259
Pleasant dreams.

00:21:54.875 --> 00:21:57.241
Computer, lights off.

00:22:19.333 --> 00:22:21.767
You're a little jumpy,
aren't you?

00:22:21.802 --> 00:22:23.360
L thought l heard something.

00:22:23.404 --> 00:22:26.339
Now you know why they
call it Demon-class.

00:22:26.373 --> 00:22:28.967
Demon implies a presence.

00:22:29.076 --> 00:22:32.204
This planetoid is unoccupied.

00:22:32.246 --> 00:22:34.646
L'm picking up the shuttlecraft.

00:22:45.559 --> 00:22:47.618
Nobody home.

00:22:47.661 --> 00:22:49.595
It's unlikely
their environmental suits

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:51.996
were able to survive
the elements for this long.

00:22:52.066 --> 00:22:53.931
L hope you're wrong.

00:23:21.028 --> 00:23:22.825
Looks like they went this way.

00:23:22.863 --> 00:23:25.627
My tricorder isn't picking up
any life signs.

00:23:25.666 --> 00:23:27.395
How did you reach
that conclusion?

00:23:27.434 --> 00:23:28.492
Footprints.

00:23:32.539 --> 00:23:35.633
L guess you never assimilated
any Indian scouts.

00:23:54.161 --> 00:23:57.426
High concentrations
of deuterium...

00:23:57.464 --> 00:23:59.625
coming from this fluid.

00:23:59.667 --> 00:24:01.567
L'll collect a sample.

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:14.777
Let's find Tom and Harry first.

00:24:14.815 --> 00:24:16.715
We'll collect
the deuterium later.

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:18.547
As you wish.

00:24:34.034 --> 00:24:37.697
Maybe they found
some shelter inside.

00:24:49.483 --> 00:24:50.609
Commander!

00:25:04.031 --> 00:25:07.125
Good to see you guys.

00:25:10.270 --> 00:25:13.000
Welcome to the Demon Planet.

00:25:24.618 --> 00:25:27.382
Our suits were corroding,
our lungs were burning...

00:25:27.421 --> 00:25:28.581
we were suffocating!

00:25:28.622 --> 00:25:29.953
You know what they say

00:25:30.023 --> 00:25:31.957
about your life
passing before your eyes?

00:25:31.992 --> 00:25:33.289
Well, it's true.

00:25:33.327 --> 00:25:34.954
L was finally
getting past puberty

00:25:35.028 --> 00:25:38.122
when suddenly,
l lost consciousness.

00:25:38.165 --> 00:25:40.599
L don't know how long
l was out, but...

00:25:40.634 --> 00:25:42.795
the next thing l knew,
l was awake

00:25:42.836 --> 00:25:45.896
and...
and l was breathing normally

00:25:45.939 --> 00:25:47.600
and l looked over at Harry.

00:25:47.641 --> 00:25:49.768
He was breathing normally, too...

00:25:49.810 --> 00:25:51.072
with his helmet off...

00:25:51.111 --> 00:25:53.602
and-and we just looked
at each other,

00:25:53.647 --> 00:25:55.547
and we just started laughing.

00:25:55.582 --> 00:25:57.209
L know it sounds crazy,

00:25:57.251 --> 00:26:00.550
but... it was
an exhilarating experience.

00:26:00.587 --> 00:26:02.851
His vital signs are normal.

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:05.916
Apparently, he has adapted.

00:26:06.026 --> 00:26:07.323
Just the same, we'd better

00:26:07.361 --> 00:26:08.919
let the Doctor
take a look at you.

00:26:09.029 --> 00:26:10.155
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:26:10.197 --> 00:26:11.596
L've already tried that.

00:26:11.632 --> 00:26:14.100
The com signal
can't get out of the caves.

00:26:14.134 --> 00:26:15.863
Then we'll call again
when we get back outside.

00:26:15.903 --> 00:26:18.371
L'm telling you, Chakotay,

00:26:18.405 --> 00:26:21.169
it was an amazing experience.

00:26:21.208 --> 00:26:24.302
It-lt's like when you're a kid
who's afraid of the water,

00:26:24.344 --> 00:26:26.778
and you suddenly realize
that you can swim.

00:26:26.814 --> 00:26:27.940
Go ahead.

00:26:28.048 --> 00:26:29.811
Take your helmets off.
Try it.

00:26:29.850 --> 00:26:31.681
L'm glad
you're feeling all right,

00:26:31.718 --> 00:26:33.948
but none of us
should be taking any risks

00:26:33.987 --> 00:26:36.046
until we know
exactly what's going on.

00:26:36.089 --> 00:26:38.057
Don't tell me
that a big, tough guy like you

00:26:38.091 --> 00:26:39.854
is afraid of a little
poisoned atmosphere.

00:26:39.893 --> 00:26:41.520
Where's Harry?

00:26:41.562 --> 00:26:43.120
He's further inside the cave.

00:26:43.163 --> 00:26:45.131
We found a huge cache
of deuterium.

00:26:45.165 --> 00:26:48.157
Let's find him and get you two
back to the ship.

00:26:48.202 --> 00:26:49.533
Whatever you say, boss,

00:26:49.570 --> 00:26:52.471
but l'm telling you, we could
breathe this air forever.

00:27:04.251 --> 00:27:05.218
Lieutenant.

00:27:05.252 --> 00:27:06.446
Yes.

00:27:06.487 --> 00:27:09.547
We should have transporters
back on line within the hour.

00:27:09.590 --> 00:27:11.455
Well, that's great,
but, right now,

00:27:11.492 --> 00:27:13.551
l'm more concerned
with little things,

00:27:13.594 --> 00:27:16.222
like, oh, l don't know,
say, life support?

00:27:16.263 --> 00:27:18.163
Indeed.
According to my calculations,

00:27:18.198 --> 00:27:20.564
environmental systems
will cease to function

00:27:20.601 --> 00:27:21.761
in two hours.

00:27:21.802 --> 00:27:23.633
You say that
like you're giving me

00:27:23.670 --> 00:27:24.830
the weather report.

00:27:24.872 --> 00:27:26.362
Well, l agree
the situation is dire,

00:27:26.406 --> 00:27:28.704
but losing our cool
will not help matters.

00:27:29.743 --> 00:27:31.870
Losing our cool?

00:27:31.912 --> 00:27:33.512
Where did you pick up
that expression?

00:27:33.645 --> 00:27:34.703
Mr. Paris.

00:27:36.615 --> 00:27:38.583
Well, there's hope for you yet.

00:27:38.617 --> 00:27:40.608
Now, how about giving me a hand?

00:27:54.032 --> 00:27:55.863
Harry.

00:27:55.901 --> 00:27:57.061
Commander.

00:27:57.102 --> 00:27:58.296
Isn't it incredible?

00:27:58.336 --> 00:28:00.896
That's what l've been
trying to tell them.

00:28:00.939 --> 00:28:02.600
Are you feeling okay, Harry?

00:28:02.641 --> 00:28:03.733
Never better.

00:28:03.775 --> 00:28:06.175
If we could get some mobile
transporters down here,

00:28:06.211 --> 00:28:07.473
we could mine enough deuterium

00:28:07.512 --> 00:28:09.605
to get us all the way to the
Alpha Quadrant and back again.

00:28:09.648 --> 00:28:12.208
Tom tells me you've already
picked up 20 kilos.

00:28:12.250 --> 00:28:15.242
That should be enough to get
the main systems back on line.

00:28:15.287 --> 00:28:17.255
Let's get back to the ship;
have the Doctor take

00:28:17.289 --> 00:28:18.278
a look at you.

00:28:18.323 --> 00:28:19.847
L'd rather stay here
and keep working,

00:28:19.891 --> 00:28:21.085
if it's all the same to you.

00:28:21.126 --> 00:28:22.252
It's not.

00:28:22.294 --> 00:28:23.818
Really, Commander, l'm fine.

00:28:23.862 --> 00:28:26.422
You should send some more
personnel out to help.

00:28:26.464 --> 00:28:28.728
They won't even need
environmental suits.

00:28:28.767 --> 00:28:30.530
L appreciate your enthusiasm,

00:28:30.569 --> 00:28:32.935
but we're going back
to Voyager... now.

00:28:32.971 --> 00:28:33.938
It's all right, Harry.

00:28:34.039 --> 00:28:36.564
Once the Doc takes a look at us
and sees we're fine,

00:28:36.608 --> 00:28:39.509
we'll get right back to work.

00:28:39.544 --> 00:28:40.738
Status, Mr. Tuvok.

00:28:40.779 --> 00:28:43.509
L've shut down life support
everywhere but Decks 1 and 5.

00:28:43.548 --> 00:28:44.572
It should provide us

00:28:44.616 --> 00:28:45.913
with an extra hour
of breathable air.

00:28:45.951 --> 00:28:47.077
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:28:47.118 --> 00:28:48.380
Janeway here.

00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:49.751
We found Tom and Harry.

00:28:49.788 --> 00:28:51.517
First good news
l've had all day.

00:28:51.556 --> 00:28:52.523
What about the deuterium?

00:28:52.557 --> 00:28:53.683
We've got a few kilos.

00:28:53.725 --> 00:28:55.590
We're on our way back
to Voyager now.

00:28:55.627 --> 00:28:56.594
What's your position?

00:28:56.628 --> 00:28:58.858
About two kilometers
from the ship.

00:28:58.897 --> 00:29:00.194
Captain...

00:29:00.231 --> 00:29:01.926
Transporters are
coming back on line.

00:29:01.967 --> 00:29:03.559
We should be able
to beam you back

00:29:03.602 --> 00:29:05.331
from that distance,
but it may take a few minutes.

00:29:05.370 --> 00:29:06.894
Have the Doctor standing by.

00:29:06.938 --> 00:29:09.839
L think he's going to want to
take a look at Tom and Harry.

00:29:22.253 --> 00:29:23.880
Computer, lights.

00:29:23.922 --> 00:29:25.549
Maximum illumination.

00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:28.218
Everybody up.

00:29:28.259 --> 00:29:29.886
Rise and shine, Mr. Neelix.

00:29:29.928 --> 00:29:31.225
What's going on?

00:29:31.262 --> 00:29:32.854
Lt's checkout time.

00:29:32.897 --> 00:29:34.524
It's the middle of the night.

00:29:34.566 --> 00:29:36.158
Medicine knows no time clock.

00:29:36.201 --> 00:29:39.796
L've got patients on the way and
there's no more room at the inn.

00:29:39.838 --> 00:29:42.068
Patients? Ls somebody sick?

00:29:42.107 --> 00:29:45.201
L can't answer that until
l've examined them, now, can I?

00:29:45.243 --> 00:29:46.835
Examine who?

00:29:46.878 --> 00:29:49.574
Ensign Kim and Lieutenant Paris.

00:29:49.614 --> 00:29:51.582
Is there anything
l can do to help?

00:29:51.616 --> 00:29:54.585
Yes. You and your friends
can vacate the premises.

00:29:54.619 --> 00:29:56.587
Right. Move!
You heard the Doctor!

00:29:56.621 --> 00:29:58.919
This is an emergency evacuation!

00:29:58.957 --> 00:30:01.187
Move! Move!

00:30:01.226 --> 00:30:02.591
Move!

00:30:02.627 --> 00:30:03.787
Doctor...

00:30:03.828 --> 00:30:05.921
Yes.

00:30:05.964 --> 00:30:07.659
Thanks for your hospitality,

00:30:07.699 --> 00:30:10.167
and if you ever need
a place to stay,

00:30:10.201 --> 00:30:11.634
my door's always open.

00:30:19.644 --> 00:30:20.975
Energizing.

00:30:33.658 --> 00:30:35.353
Beam Tom and Harry to Sick Bay.

00:30:43.001 --> 00:30:44.127
What happened to them?

00:30:44.169 --> 00:30:46.729
As soon as we beamed aboard,
they started suffocating.

00:30:46.771 --> 00:30:48.602
Computer, erect
a level-7 force field

00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:49.868
around bio-beds 1 and 2.

00:30:49.908 --> 00:30:51.000
Force field established.

00:30:51.076 --> 00:30:52.008
What are you doing?

00:30:52.110 --> 00:30:54.169
Filling the area
inside the force field

00:30:54.212 --> 00:30:56.544
with the atmospheric gases
from the planet.

00:30:56.581 --> 00:30:58.640
Try to breathe normally now.

00:30:58.683 --> 00:31:00.981
Easy, or you'll hyperventilate.

00:31:03.288 --> 00:31:05.586
Slowly, in and out.

00:31:05.623 --> 00:31:08.217
In... and out.

00:31:11.596 --> 00:31:13.757
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:31:13.798 --> 00:31:17.097
The Doctor continues
to investigate Tom and Harry

00:31:17.135 --> 00:31:20.502
whose condition seems
as serious as it is strange.

00:31:20.538 --> 00:31:22.301
That stuff is in our blood?

00:31:22.340 --> 00:31:23.602
L'm afraid so.

00:31:23.641 --> 00:31:27.133
From what l can tell,
you've been bioformed.

00:31:27.178 --> 00:31:28.406
Bioformed?

00:31:28.446 --> 00:31:30.744
Think of it as the opposite
of terraforming.

00:31:30.782 --> 00:31:32.807
In the same way we adapt
the environment of a planet

00:31:32.851 --> 00:31:36.480
to suit our needs,
this planet...

00:31:36.521 --> 00:31:37.749
has adapted you.

00:31:37.789 --> 00:31:39.313
How is that possible?

00:31:39.357 --> 00:31:41.917
This fluid somehow
entered your bloodstream

00:31:41.960 --> 00:31:43.985
and began altering
your physiology

00:31:44.028 --> 00:31:45.393
at the cellular level.

00:31:45.430 --> 00:31:47.864
L haven't had the time
to analyze the substance,

00:31:47.899 --> 00:31:48.991
but l hope to have
some answers soon.

00:31:49.067 --> 00:31:50.159
L'd like to run

00:31:50.201 --> 00:31:52.294
a few tests of my own,
if you don't mind.

00:31:52.337 --> 00:31:53.634
Of course.

00:31:53.671 --> 00:31:55.866
So, what's our prognosis, Doc?

00:31:55.907 --> 00:31:58.432
Well...

00:31:58.476 --> 00:32:00.501
you'll be fine.

00:32:00.545 --> 00:32:03.139
As long as you keep breathing
the planet's gases.

00:32:03.181 --> 00:32:06.912
You mean we have to stay
inside this force field?

00:32:06.951 --> 00:32:08.942
L'm afraid
it's worse than that.

00:32:08.987 --> 00:32:12.548
The atmosphere of this planet
can't be replicated safely.

00:32:12.590 --> 00:32:14.251
Which means...

00:32:14.292 --> 00:32:16.590
if we leave...

00:32:16.628 --> 00:32:19.153
we'll have nothing to breathe.

00:32:19.197 --> 00:32:20.596
Exactly.

00:32:20.632 --> 00:32:23.624
Either we find a way
to treat your condition...

00:32:25.637 --> 00:32:27.696
...or you'll have
to be left behind.

00:32:42.654 --> 00:32:44.986
Can the bioforming
process be reversed?

00:32:45.023 --> 00:32:46.320
As it stands,

00:32:46.357 --> 00:32:49.155
l don't know enough about
the phenomenon to undo it.

00:32:49.194 --> 00:32:51.754
L'll send Chakotay and
Seven back to the surface.

00:32:51.796 --> 00:32:54.196
They'll gather as much
information as they can.

00:32:54.232 --> 00:32:56.530
B'Elanna and l will start
running tests on this.

00:32:56.568 --> 00:32:58.593
Let me go with the away team,
Captain.

00:32:58.636 --> 00:33:00.297
L know the terrain.
L can help.

00:33:00.338 --> 00:33:01.737
Doctor?

00:33:01.773 --> 00:33:03.240
Right now, they're
better off out there

00:33:03.274 --> 00:33:04.536
than they are in here.

00:33:04.576 --> 00:33:06.339
But one of you will
have to remain,

00:33:06.377 --> 00:33:08.106
so l can monitor your condition.

00:33:08.146 --> 00:33:09.408
No problem.

00:33:09.447 --> 00:33:12.610
L volunteer Tom to stay here
and play guinea pig.

00:33:19.858 --> 00:33:22.486
Each square kilometer
of this planetoid

00:33:22.527 --> 00:33:24.893
is less appealing than the last.

00:33:26.264 --> 00:33:28.459
L think it's breathtaking.

00:33:28.499 --> 00:33:30.126
Breathtaking?

00:33:30.168 --> 00:33:31.499
Yes.

00:33:31.536 --> 00:33:34.937
Perhaps your recent experience
has impaired your perceptions.

00:33:34.973 --> 00:33:37.203
No, l don't think so.

00:33:37.242 --> 00:33:40.143
L wasn't really
seeing it before.

00:33:40.178 --> 00:33:41.941
Seeing what?

00:33:41.980 --> 00:33:43.538
The beauty.

00:33:43.581 --> 00:33:47.278
Would you care
to point out an example?

00:33:47.318 --> 00:33:49.548
Look over there.

00:33:49.587 --> 00:33:51.885
What do you see?

00:33:51.923 --> 00:33:54.391
L see monochromatic
geological formations,

00:33:54.425 --> 00:33:56.484
dust, haze.

00:33:56.527 --> 00:33:57.926
What do you see, Harry?

00:33:57.962 --> 00:34:00.760
To me,
those geological formations

00:34:00.798 --> 00:34:03.358
are a dozen shades
of red and gold.

00:34:03.401 --> 00:34:07.895
That dust... it's glowing

00:34:07.939 --> 00:34:13.400
and the haze... it seems
to intensify the colors.

00:34:13.444 --> 00:34:15.935
L'm sorry.

00:34:15.980 --> 00:34:19.211
L know it's weird, but l feel
connected to this place.

00:34:19.250 --> 00:34:20.478
Connected how?

00:34:20.518 --> 00:34:22.713
L'm picking up
humanoid life signs.

00:34:22.754 --> 00:34:24.415
Location?

00:34:24.455 --> 00:34:26.582
100 meters this way.

00:34:31.429 --> 00:34:34.932
Magnify, factor 10.

00:34:35.065 --> 00:34:37.590
Deuterium, hydrogen sulfate,
dichromates.

00:34:37.634 --> 00:34:39.261
Add a little sodium chloride

00:34:39.303 --> 00:34:42.272
and it would probably taste
a lot like Neelix's soup.

00:34:42.306 --> 00:34:44.934
We should be so lucky.

00:34:44.975 --> 00:34:46.408
Oh, what's this?

00:34:46.443 --> 00:34:48.968
Magnify, factor 20.

00:34:51.481 --> 00:34:52.948
Captain?

00:34:56.186 --> 00:34:58.552
That's a protein molecule.

00:34:58.588 --> 00:35:00.351
This fluid has
organic properties.

00:35:00.390 --> 00:35:03.382
Let me see the sample that's
been treated with the reagents.

00:35:07.464 --> 00:35:09.728
Captain...

00:35:13.270 --> 00:35:15.135
Let's get you to Sick Bay.

00:35:15.172 --> 00:35:17.436
Wait.
That might not be necessary.

00:35:52.509 --> 00:35:53.999
Commander!

00:36:20.470 --> 00:36:21.937
Janeway to Bridge.
Report.

00:36:22.039 --> 00:36:24.064
A large pool
of the metallic compound

00:36:24.107 --> 00:36:25.665
is forming beneath the ship.

00:36:25.709 --> 00:36:27.040
We are sinking, Captain.

00:36:27.077 --> 00:36:28.567
On my way.
Get down to Engineering.

00:36:28.612 --> 00:36:29.340
Get thrusters on line.

00:36:29.379 --> 00:36:30.437
We're getting off this planet.

00:36:31.681 --> 00:36:33.546
L'm not sure how,
but they're still alive.

00:36:33.583 --> 00:36:35.278
Just barely.

00:36:35.318 --> 00:36:36.512
Tuvok to Chakotay.

00:36:36.553 --> 00:36:37.713
Go ahead.

00:36:37.754 --> 00:36:39.949
The Captain has ordered
an emergency ascent.

00:36:40.023 --> 00:36:41.820
We must bring you
back to the ship.

00:36:41.858 --> 00:36:43.519
Understood.
L've got five to beam back.

00:36:43.560 --> 00:36:44.652
Five?!

00:36:44.694 --> 00:36:47.219
We found another Paris and Kim.

00:36:47.264 --> 00:36:48.731
L can't explain it.

00:36:48.765 --> 00:36:50.858
L think l can.
Prepare for transport.

00:36:50.901 --> 00:36:52.596
Beam us directly to Sick Bay.

00:36:52.636 --> 00:36:53.967
No.

00:36:54.004 --> 00:36:55.369
L don't want to go back.

00:36:55.405 --> 00:36:56.633
Transporters are still
acting up.

00:36:56.673 --> 00:36:57.901
We can't get individual locks.

00:36:57.941 --> 00:37:00.205
We're going to have to grab you
in a wide beam,

00:37:00.243 --> 00:37:01.733
and bring you in as a group.

00:37:01.778 --> 00:37:02.836
Acknowledged.

00:37:05.315 --> 00:37:06.543
L belong here.

00:37:06.583 --> 00:37:07.845
Maybe so,

00:37:07.884 --> 00:37:09.647
but until we know
what's going on,

00:37:09.686 --> 00:37:11.347
you've got to come back
with us to the ship.

00:37:14.157 --> 00:37:15.055
Harry, no!

00:37:20.397 --> 00:37:22.797
Four of the away team
are in Sick Bay, Captain.

00:37:22.833 --> 00:37:25.165
L'm trying to get a lock
on the fifth.

00:37:25.202 --> 00:37:26.669
It is Ensign Kim,

00:37:26.703 --> 00:37:29.194
or rather,
one of the Ensigns Kim.

00:37:29.239 --> 00:37:30.672
The ship is
continuing to sink.

00:37:30.707 --> 00:37:31.674
Then there's no time.

00:37:31.708 --> 00:37:32.766
We've got to get back
into orbit.

00:37:32.809 --> 00:37:33.776
We'll worry about Harry,

00:37:33.810 --> 00:37:35.334
or whoever he is, once we're up.

00:37:35.378 --> 00:37:37.846
Bring antigrav thrusters
on line.

00:37:37.881 --> 00:37:39.542
Thrusters enabled.

00:37:39.583 --> 00:37:41.881
Inertial dampers
to flight configuration.

00:37:41.918 --> 00:37:43.317
Dampers reconfigured.

00:37:43.353 --> 00:37:44.877
All stations report ready.

00:37:44.921 --> 00:37:47.048
Initiating ascent.

00:37:47.090 --> 00:37:49.923
L need power to the thrusters.

00:37:49.960 --> 00:37:52.622
We are being restrained
by an electromagnetic force.

00:37:52.662 --> 00:37:53.754
Compensate.

00:37:54.798 --> 00:37:56.766
No effect.

00:37:56.800 --> 00:37:59.291
Decks 14 and 15 are submerged.

00:37:59.336 --> 00:38:01.236
The ship is continuing to sink.

00:38:13.250 --> 00:38:14.410
Report.

00:38:14.451 --> 00:38:16.248
Thrusters are off-line
due to an overload.

00:38:16.286 --> 00:38:18.720
Decks 13 through 15
are submerged.

00:38:18.755 --> 00:38:21.883
If we don't lift off soon,
the hull will begin to corrode.

00:38:21.925 --> 00:38:23.358
Bridge to Engineering.

00:38:23.393 --> 00:38:24.417
Ensign Vorik here.

00:38:24.461 --> 00:38:25.792
L need thrusters back on line.

00:38:25.829 --> 00:38:27.353
Lieutenant Torres
has already sent a team

00:38:27.397 --> 00:38:28.659
to the thruster control
junction.

00:38:28.698 --> 00:38:29.665
How long?

00:38:29.699 --> 00:38:30.927
At least a half an hour.

00:38:31.034 --> 00:38:33.434
Even if thrusters are repaired,
they

00:38:33.470 --> 00:38:35.563
won't be of much use
if we sink any deeper.

00:38:37.107 --> 00:38:38.768
There must be some way
to disperse it.

00:38:40.243 --> 00:38:43.110
Try a nadion burst
from the phaser emitters.

00:38:43.146 --> 00:38:44.807
It may weaken the
electromagnetic properties

00:38:44.848 --> 00:38:45.872
of the fluid.

00:38:45.916 --> 00:38:46.940
Aye, Captain.

00:38:47.050 --> 00:38:49.780
L'm on my way to Sick Bay
to check on Harry and Tom.

00:38:49.819 --> 00:38:51.218
You've got the Bridge.

00:39:00.397 --> 00:39:01.728
How are they?

00:39:01.765 --> 00:39:04.700
Lucky. The backup systems
in their environmental suits

00:39:04.734 --> 00:39:06.531
kept their
vital functions going.

00:39:06.570 --> 00:39:08.538
It'll take time,
but they'll recover.

00:39:08.572 --> 00:39:09.834
And him?

00:39:09.873 --> 00:39:11.465
Aside from his ability

00:39:11.508 --> 00:39:13.874
to breathe the rarefied air
on this planet,

00:39:13.910 --> 00:39:15.901
he's the exact duplicate
of Mr. Paris.

00:39:15.946 --> 00:39:17.914
He even seems to share
his memories,

00:39:17.948 --> 00:39:20.007
not to mention
his winning personality.

00:39:20.050 --> 00:39:21.449
B'Elanna and l discovered

00:39:21.484 --> 00:39:23.714
that the fluid
has mimetic properties.

00:39:23.753 --> 00:39:25.880
Somehow, it reads the DNA

00:39:25.922 --> 00:39:28.220
of whatever
it comes in contact with

00:39:28.258 --> 00:39:30.158
and re-creates it.

00:39:30.193 --> 00:39:31.182
Fascinating.

00:39:36.466 --> 00:39:38.559
Can you tell me who you are?

00:39:38.602 --> 00:39:40.934
Please... just let me go back.

00:39:40.971 --> 00:39:43.166
Not until l find out
why two of my crew

00:39:43.206 --> 00:39:44.503
have been duplicated.

00:39:44.541 --> 00:39:46.441
Captain, you have to believe me.

00:39:46.476 --> 00:39:49.206
L don't know any more
than you do about this.

00:39:49.246 --> 00:39:51.942
Until he showed up,
l thought l was Tom Paris.

00:39:52.015 --> 00:39:54.779
A little changed by my
experience on the planet maybe,

00:39:54.818 --> 00:39:57.218
but now l don't know
who or what l am.

00:39:57.254 --> 00:40:00.052
All l know is that
l have to get off this ship

00:40:00.090 --> 00:40:02.217
and go back down
to the surface.

00:40:02.259 --> 00:40:04.625
We're ready to try
the nadion burst, Captain.

00:40:04.661 --> 00:40:05.787
Do it.

00:40:08.732 --> 00:40:10.063
What are you doing?!

00:40:10.100 --> 00:40:12.227
Captain, we're receiving
an urgent hail.

00:40:12.269 --> 00:40:15.136
It's from Ensign Kim...
the one on the surface.

00:40:15.171 --> 00:40:16.195
Put him through.

00:40:16.239 --> 00:40:17.706
Captain, please!

00:40:17.741 --> 00:40:19.333
Stop what you're doing!

00:40:19.376 --> 00:40:22.106
Lf you really do have
Harry Kim's memories,

00:40:22.145 --> 00:40:23.874
you know that l'm going to do
whatever it takes

00:40:23.913 --> 00:40:25.642
to get this ship back in orbit.

00:40:25.682 --> 00:40:26.979
You can't do that!

00:40:27.017 --> 00:40:28.143
Why not?

00:40:28.184 --> 00:40:31.381
I... l'm not sure
l understand it myself.

00:40:31.421 --> 00:40:34.720
Well, then you're going to have
to help me figure it out.

00:40:34.758 --> 00:40:37.921
Mr. Tuvok, l'm on my way
to Transporter Room 1.

00:40:37.961 --> 00:40:41.158
Erect a level-7 force field
around the platform.

00:40:41.197 --> 00:40:43.688
Fill it with atmosphere
from the planet

00:40:43.733 --> 00:40:47.499
and then beam Mr. Kim,
or rather his duplicate, aboard.

00:40:47.537 --> 00:40:48.629
Aye, Captain.

00:40:54.978 --> 00:40:56.002
Do you have a lock on him?

00:40:56.046 --> 00:40:57.013
Yes, ma'am.

00:40:57.047 --> 00:40:58.036
Energize.

00:41:03.253 --> 00:41:04.948
Release my vessel.

00:41:05.055 --> 00:41:05.953
We can't do that.

00:41:06.056 --> 00:41:07.785
"We"?

00:41:07.824 --> 00:41:12.921
The planet and I,
we're connected somehow.

00:41:12.962 --> 00:41:14.088
L can't explain it, Captain.

00:41:14.130 --> 00:41:15.358
L only know
that you've got to stop.

00:41:15.398 --> 00:41:16.797
And l'm willing to stop,

00:41:16.833 --> 00:41:19.199
but l'll say it again:
Release the ship.

00:41:19.235 --> 00:41:21.533
No. We need you.

00:41:21.571 --> 00:41:23.801
Janeway to Tuvok.
Fire.

00:41:30.080 --> 00:41:31.308
What are you?

00:41:31.348 --> 00:41:32.975
Stop. No.

00:41:33.016 --> 00:41:33.914
L'll fire again.

00:41:33.950 --> 00:41:35.150
You're killing us.

00:41:35.283 --> 00:41:36.443
You're leaving me no choice.

00:41:36.484 --> 00:41:38.111
It's not fair. It's wrong!

00:41:38.153 --> 00:41:39.484
Janeway to Tuvok...

00:41:39.521 --> 00:41:41.079
No!

00:41:41.122 --> 00:41:42.783
No, no, no.

00:41:42.824 --> 00:41:45.657
Please... no more.

00:41:45.693 --> 00:41:46.819
Hold your fire, Tuvok.

00:41:46.861 --> 00:41:48.920
Captain, we are continuing
to submerge.

00:41:48.963 --> 00:41:49.930
Hold your fire.

00:41:49.964 --> 00:41:51.431
Acknowledged.

00:41:51.466 --> 00:41:52.956
L want some answers.

00:41:53.001 --> 00:41:56.437
L'm trying to understand.

00:41:56.471 --> 00:41:58.405
This is hard for me as well.

00:41:58.439 --> 00:42:00.907
You said you have
a connection to this planet.

00:42:00.942 --> 00:42:02.807
You talk about it
like it's alive.

00:42:02.844 --> 00:42:04.175
Alive?

00:42:06.481 --> 00:42:09.109
Yes...

00:42:09.150 --> 00:42:10.811
but not the planet.

00:42:12.654 --> 00:42:14.315
The silver blood.

00:42:14.355 --> 00:42:17.950
The compound that sampled
Harry's DNA...

00:42:17.992 --> 00:42:20.085
and created you.

00:42:20.128 --> 00:42:24.622
Yes... but it's never been
conscious, never sentient

00:42:24.666 --> 00:42:27.829
before now...
before me and the other.

00:42:27.869 --> 00:42:29.200
Tom Paris.

00:42:29.237 --> 00:42:30.636
We're the first.

00:42:30.672 --> 00:42:31.730
Don't you see?

00:42:31.773 --> 00:42:32.740
You came here.

00:42:32.774 --> 00:42:34.105
You showed us.

00:42:34.142 --> 00:42:38.806
When the compound came in
contact with Tom and Harry,

00:42:38.846 --> 00:42:42.304
it experienced awareness
for the first time.

00:42:42.350 --> 00:42:46.548
Before, it was only instinct...

00:42:46.588 --> 00:42:48.613
sound and light and heat.

00:42:50.858 --> 00:42:54.692
But those two...
showed us thought.

00:42:54.729 --> 00:42:56.959
L'm beginning to understand.

00:43:00.235 --> 00:43:03.363
This silver blood...

00:43:03.404 --> 00:43:06.703
experienced sentience...

00:43:06.741 --> 00:43:09.767
and now you want more.

00:43:09.811 --> 00:43:13.338
You want to duplicate
the rest of this crew

00:43:13.381 --> 00:43:15.349
and populate this planet.

00:43:15.383 --> 00:43:18.181
You're trying so hard
to reach home, but...

00:43:18.219 --> 00:43:19.846
this can be home.

00:43:19.887 --> 00:43:22.117
Not for me
and not for my people.

00:43:22.156 --> 00:43:24.818
Do you understand
why we can't stay here?

00:43:26.094 --> 00:43:27.755
L think so.

00:43:29.597 --> 00:43:32.065
Well, then release us.

00:43:32.100 --> 00:43:34.091
We'd rather die than be alone.

00:43:36.638 --> 00:43:39.072
We deserve life.

00:43:45.179 --> 00:43:47.511
This silver blood
that created you...

00:43:50.451 --> 00:43:53.443
...it duplicated Harry
without killing him.

00:43:56.124 --> 00:43:59.423
So you don't need our bodies...

00:43:59.460 --> 00:44:01.451
only samples of DNA.

00:44:07.468 --> 00:44:10.437
Release Voyager...

00:44:10.471 --> 00:44:12.769
and l'll speak to my crew.

00:44:12.807 --> 00:44:14.604
And if they're willing,

00:44:14.642 --> 00:44:17.202
l'll let you duplicate
the rest of us.

00:44:18.980 --> 00:44:20.140
Bridge to Janeway.

00:44:20.181 --> 00:44:21.341
We've stopped, Captain.

00:44:21.382 --> 00:44:22.576
We're no longer submerging.

00:44:22.617 --> 00:44:24.312
Understood.

00:44:24.352 --> 00:44:25.478
We're getting out of here,
Tuvok,

00:44:25.520 --> 00:44:29.456
but first, assemble the crew
in Cargo Bay 1,

00:44:29.490 --> 00:44:31.651
and have the Doctor
meet me there.

00:44:31.693 --> 00:44:32.591
Captain?

00:44:32.627 --> 00:44:33.616
L'll explain later.

00:44:38.666 --> 00:44:41.157
It's time to meet
your new family.

00:44:48.042 --> 00:44:50.067
All stations report
ready for liftoff.

00:44:50.111 --> 00:44:51.908
Code Blue status confirmed.

00:44:51.946 --> 00:44:53.413
Take us up, Mr. Paris.

00:44:53.448 --> 00:44:54.779
Aye, Captain.
